# Code owners for CI and agent configuration.
#
# Why this file exists: on a `pull_request` event GitHub runs the PR's own copy
# of the workflow files, and of any local composite action (`uses: ./...`) they
# call out of the PR's checkout. A pull request can therefore rewrite the logic
# behind a required status check and have it report success while the real jobs
# are broken. Nothing inside a workflow closes that, because the workflow itself
# is equally PR-controlled - so human review of these paths is the control.
#
# The same reasoning covers the files agents load as instructions: an unreviewed
# edit there redirects what every future agent run does.
#
# This takes effect only when branch protection (or a ruleset) on the default
# branch has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. Without that toggle
# these entries request reviewers but block nothing.

# Workflows, composite actions, and the Copilot-side instructions/skills/agents.
/.github/       @rajbos @FokkoVeegens

# The Claude Code side of the same configuration. AGENTS.md requires these to be
# kept mirrored with their .github/ counterparts, and Claude Code loads them
# automatically - so they need the same review as the files they mirror.
/.claude/       @rajbos @FokkoVeegens

# Repository-wide agent instructions. Every coding agent reads these at the
# start of a run.
/AGENTS.md      @rajbos @FokkoVeegens
/CLAUDE.md      @rajbos @FokkoVeegens

# The devcontainer runs commands, and `initializeCommand` runs them on the
# developer's own machine before the container is even built - an edit here
# executes on a host, not just in CI.
/.devcontainer/ @rajbos @FokkoVeegens
